      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Consider adding a volatile, superstitious hitwoman who speaks in fragmented metaphors to contrast your detective's analytical precision, forcing him to constantly rely on her chaotic intuition for survival. You could also introduce a slick, manipulative corporate fixer whose polished exterior hides a brutal underworld network that exploits the city's shadows. Finally, a weary, drug-addicted informant who stole a layout from your main character first could create immediate personal stakes and challenge his moral code head-on. These three figures will collectively highlight his intellectual isolation while driving the narrative toward catastrophic consequences.",
